comments[4]:
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T20:35:42.930Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus3157 with no omissions or unreadable records, request-specific GH-number and semantic searches, current open/in_progress inventories, and full live predecessor data/comments/history. The predecessor scope is delivered; this report names a distinct boundary. New intake is open and unclaimed. Source report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1628"
  - created_at: "2026-10-31T00:26:34.405Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Reproduced on current source (branch base 1a72d089d, built SDK): create closed item, then update(id, {title, status: closed, closeReason: same, force: true}) -> closureChanged=true, clockChanged=true (closed_at 00:17:26.978Z -> 00:17:27.105Z, updated_at -> 00:17:27.110Z). Open-item control with an identical payload: clockChanged=false. Root cause: routeCloseStatusUpdate in src/sdk/lifecycle/update.ts sends any update naming the close status to runClose without checking whether the item is already closed; mutateCloseMetadata then re-stamps closed_at unconditionally and closeItem passes no skipNoop, so item-store stamps updated_at. commitItemMutations reuses update(), so the transaction path shares the defect; update-many already compared before routing and was unaffected."
  - created_at: "2026-10-31T00:26:34.927Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Fix: routeCloseStatusUpdate now reads the stored item and, when the requested close status, trimmed reason and completed_at already describe it, applies only the remaining fields through the ordinary update path (skipNoop) and reports terminal_state_unchanged; a bare identical update returns changed_fields [] without force. A different reason remains a repeat closure routed to runClose with the existing force gate. After the fix the same repro reports closureChanged=false, clockChanged=false. Negative control: with src/sdk/lifecycle/update.ts stashed, 3 of the 4 new update-command tests fail (changed_fields [status, closed_at, close_reason] vs []); the fourth guards the preserved repeat-closure behaviour and passes both ways. Mixed-batch retry test on commitItemMutations keeps closed_at/updated_at byte-identical across two commits."
  - created_at: "2026-10-31T08:38:58.578Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Review follow-up on PR #1637 (CodeRabbit, 2026-10-31): two correctness gaps in the repeated-terminal-state no-op path, both fixed with regression tests.\n\n1. **Blank reason under required-reason governance.** `describesCurrentTerminalState` normalized a whitespace-only `--close-reason` to \"absent\", so with `governance.require_close_reason` enabled an already-closed item answered `terminal_state_unchanged` while the same blank reason on an open item is refused with `close_reason_required`. The predicate now takes `requireCloseReason` and returns false for a supplied-but-blank reason only when a reason is required, so the close route refuses it. With the reason optional the blank value stays a no-op (routing it would re-stamp `closed_at`, the defect this item fixed).\n2. **Concurrent reopen between classification and the field write.** The classification read holds no item lock. If another writer reopened the item before the title-only retry, the retry dropped `status` and the request reported `terminal_state_unchanged` on an open item. `applyRepeatedTerminalStateUpdate` now checks the status the locked write returned and hands a reopened item to the closure writer (`closeRoutedItem`, the same helper the ordinary route now shares), so the request is never silently downgraded.\n\nAlso covered: a changed `--completed-at` is a closure and its exact repeat a no-op; a routed close for a missing id refuses with the shared not-found guidance. `docs/COMMANDS.md` now states that other requested fields move `updated_at` and write history only when they change a stored value.\n\nEvidence: `tests/unit/commands/lifecycle/update-command.spec.ts` (GH-1628 block, 8 cases) and module coverage 100% lines/branches for `src/sdk/lifecycle/repeated-terminal-state.ts`.\n\nReview of the landing PR #1638 (CodeRabbit, 2026-10-31, rated Major): on a closed item, `--status closed --unset close-reason` took the repeated-state path and succeeded, removing a reason that `governance.require_close_reason` requires. `assertRoutedCloseKeepsRequiredReason` (in `repeated-terminal-state.ts`) now refuses such a request with the closure writer's own `close_reason_required` before either route can write, detecting the unset with the update parser's tokenization and the shared `CLOSE_REASON_UNSET_ALIASES`. The repeated-state path also re-checks the reason and completion time, not only the status, on the item the locked field write returned, and hands any divergence to the closure writer. Tests: \"refuses unsetting a required close reason on a closed item before any write\" (fails without the guard; bytes, reason and history unchanged) and \"hands the request to the closure writer when the reason changed under the lock\"."
    edited_at: "2026-10-31T14:19:52.500Z"
